    "description": "FirstLight USA, LLC is the U.S. generation platform operating under the FirstLight Power brand. Its portfolio includes run-of-river hydroelectric plants, the Northfield Mountain pumped-storage facility, solar generation and battery storage across Massachusetts, Connecticut and Pennsylvania. Energy Capital Partners created the platform in 2006, GDF SUEZ/ENGIE owned it from 2008 to 2016, and PSP Investments acquired 100% on June 1, 2016. PSP signed a sale of the U.S. operations to Hull Street Energy on May 19, 2026, but the transfer had not legally closed as of September 1, 2026; PSP therefore remains the active owner and Hull Street is pending only. Canadian H2O Power and Hydromega assets, individual projects, subsidiaries and issuers are outside the canonical U.S. platform boundary.",
